          "note": "Topic 4.1.5.4 Print Spooling (PDF 104-105, printed 101-102)."
        }
      ],
      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Print spooling manages print jobs sent to a printer. Documents are placed in a queue in order of arrival, so the first document sent is printed first and the others wait their turn. This prevents documents printing out of sequence or clashing when sent at the same time."
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
